@startuml 08_feedback_control_method

title Feedback Control Method - Hierarchy

abstract class FeedbackControlMethod {
  +init_cov_state(problem_def) : <internal>
  +augment_error_dynamics(error_dynamics) : ErrorDynamics
  +propagate_cov(error_dynamics, cov_state, problem_def) : ErrorState
}

class TrueStateFeedback {
  +init_cov_state(problem_def) : <internal>
  +augment_error_dynamics(error_dynamics) : ErrorDynamics
  +propagate_cov(error_dynamics, cov_state, problem_def) : ErrorState
}

class EstimatedStateFeedback {
  -measurement_model : MeasurementModel
  +init_cov_state(problem_def) : <internal>
  +augment_error_dynamics(error_dynamics) : ErrorDynamics
  +propagate_cov(error_dynamics, cov_state, problem_def) : ErrorState
}

note right of TrueStateFeedback
  Internal cov_state here is P_hst (7x7).
  augment_error_dynamics is a no-op (Null
  Object pattern) - returns error_dynamics
  unchanged, since no measurement model is
  needed.
  propagate_cov implements the
  "TrueStateFeedback_CovPropagators"
  sub-arc iterator from dynamics.py, and
  returns ErrorState(P_hst, P_U_arc_hst)
  directly - P_hst IS the internal state.
end note

note right of EstimatedStateFeedback
  augment_error_dynamics populates
  error_dynamics.H_hst / P_v_hst from
  measurement_model (these are zero-filled
  placeholders coming out of
  SensitivityPropagator).

  Internal cov_state here is Paug_hst (14x14
  augmented form: Phat/Ptild blocks), plus
  L_js (EKF gain history) - both private to
  this class, never exposed.
  propagate_cov implements the
  "EstimatedStateFeedback_CovPropagators"
  sub-arc iterator (incl. EKF measurement
  update, using error_dynamics.H_hst/P_v_hst),
  then derives at each node
    P_hst = Phat - Phattild - Phattild.T + Ptild
  and returns ErrorState(P_hst, P_U_arc_hst) -
  same shape as TrueStateFeedback.
end note

FeedbackControlMethod <|-- TrueStateFeedback
FeedbackControlMethod <|-- EstimatedStateFeedback

note bottom of FeedbackControlMethod
  objective_term() and
  covariance_constraint_value() are
  intentionally NOT part of this interface.
  Because ErrorState is standardized
  (see 01_data_structures.puml), the
  objective/constraint math that consumes
  P_hst/P_U_arc_hst is identical regardless
  of which controller produced it - it lives
  as plain functions / Constraint subclasses
  operating on (inputs, traj_state, error_state,
  problem_def), with no reference back to
  the controller.
end note

note "K_arc_hst and G_exe_arc_hst are fields of\nerror_dynamics by the time propagate_cov() is\ncalled (populated by gain_param.compute_gains()\nand a free function respectively - see\n09_stochastic_top_composition.puml and\n01_data_structures.puml)." as N2
FeedbackControlMethod .. N2

note "Future extension point:\ne.g. a square-root-form feedback method\ncould be added here without\nchanging StochasticTOP - it would just\nproduce ErrorState the same way internally." as N1
FeedbackControlMethod .. N1

@enduml
